set.body:
Objective

Turn evidence-sampling-v1 into a statistically validated, query-first calibration layer for estimated evidence pairings without changing the evidence estimand or creating method-specific inference engines.

Constitution

The point estimator remains E_hat(H,K). Its sampling law is V_ab = Cov[E_hat(H_a,K_a), E_hat(H_b,K_b)]. relation remains the pure algebraic object; relation_fit or an identity-bound external error channel supplies sampling capabilities. Generalization edges are estimator contributions, not independent replicates. Calibration targets and metric uncertainty remain explicit.

Program acceptance

- fixed-metric equal-partition crossvalidated distance covariance matches Diedrichsen et al. Eq. 13 and an independent oracle;
- the complete distance covariance and exact linear transports are queryable without mandatory dense materialization;
- public relation_fit workflows produce calibrated local uncertainty under declared assumptions;
- precomputed relations refuse with an explanatory capability message;
- learned, heterogeneous, and spatial covariance regimes are admitted only after their own laws and evidence;
- product-oracle, generative coverage, and realistic runtime/memory gates pass; and
- documentation states the estimator, target, assumptions, and unavailable capabilities without novelty framing.

Non-goals

No classifier zoo, generic inference registry, automatic spatial random-field claim, silent learned-metric conditioning, or population inference is authorized by this epic.
